================================================================================
Why BSD-3-Clause (decided 2026-10-15, at the repository's creation)
================================================================================

The references are NumPy, SciPy and scikit-image, all BSD-3-Clause. They are
oracles: their code is run beside the kit, never copied into it. The Swift seed
of slice 1 is the copyright holder's own code from the owner's GPL-3.0 applications
(below), relicensed here; the owner confirms that relicensing before the
first push (docs/status.md, "Waiting"). Should the owner decline, the package becomes
GPL-3.0 like the suite's other kits, by replacing LICENSE and this paragraph.

GPL-3.0 sources (Atomap for atom-column finding, HyperSpy, py4DSTEM) are not
ported into ImagoCore, ImagoFFT, ImagoFilters or ImagoAlignment. A later port of
one goes into its own module, licensed GPL-3.0 and named as such in
Package.swift and the README, or into a separate package; one GPL module never
changes the licence of the others, but an application linking it is bound by it.


